From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 06:57:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ports/arkweb: wire the OHOS system clipboard via
 ohos-pasteboard

On the ohos target the clipboard delegate used only an in-process fallback
that does not cross processes. Add an ohos branch to clipboard_delegate.rs
that uses the ohos-pasteboard crate (the OHOS analogue of arboard), keeping
the in-process fallback on error, and enable the `clipboard` feature for the
arkweb servo dependency so both arkweb and servoshell-ohos get it.

ohos-pasteboard is taken from crates.io, as are its own dependencies
(ohos-pasteboard-sys and udmf, both from openharmony-rs); the lockfile is
updated accordingly, which `mach build --locked` needs. It is only pulled in
under cfg(target_env = "ohos").

Enable the dom_async_clipboard_enabled pref for arkweb so web content can
reach the clipboard via navigator.clipboard (off by default in Servo). Log
a warning when the OHOS pasteboard path errors and falls back to the
in-process store.

Reading the OHOS pasteboard needs ohos.permission.READ_PASTEBOARD, which is
grantMode user_grant / availableLevel system_basic -- a normal-APL app can't
hold it. Declare it in the test app (module.json5 + reason string) and
re-provision the debug signing profile at system_basic APL with the
permission in its ACL, so it can be granted via atm on the (developer-mode)
test device.

Verified on device: navigator.clipboard writeText->readText round-trips
'SERVOCLIP42' through the real system pasteboard, no in-process fallback;
without READ_PASTEBOARD, get_text returns status 201 and falls back.

Validation: Test by running ./mach build --locked --ohos, then on device: navigator.clipboard.writeText/readText must round-trip through the system pasteboard (grant READ_PASTEBOARD via atm first); no automated test yet.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; implementation and on-device testing)
